  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Maria bought $1$ cup of olive oil and paid $$1.50$ for it. What's the unit price per gallon?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ cups in one gallon.",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that there are $16$ cups in each gallon.  \n\nSince the price is $$1.50$ per cup, to find the price per gallon, we multiply by $16:$\n\n$$\n1.50\\times 16=24\n$$\n\nTherefore, the olive oil costs $$24$ per gallon.",
